# ─── The provider ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# base_url + api_key IS the entire integration. That is not a boast — it is why docs/DECISIONS.md
# D01 refuses a framework. Swap these two lines and the agent, the ledgers, the gates, the cache
# and the 4,480-run eval harness all keep working, unchanged.

# (a) Nebius Token Factory — what the 4,480-run evaluation was actually measured on
LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.tokenfactory.nebius.com/v1/
LLM_API_KEY=

# (b) YOUR OWN GPU — and what the live demo actually runs on.
#     `uv run modal secret create research-agent-llm LLM_API_KEY=<pick-one>`
#     `uv run modal deploy infra/modal_vllm.py`
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://<you>--research-agent-vllm-serve.modal.run/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=<the same value you put in the Modal secret>
# AGENT_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507
# VERIFIER_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507
#   Deployed and verified: the full agent — contract, ledger, all four gates — runs against this
#   and gets the Simpson's-paradox task RIGHT (+0.150, dodging the -0.087 confounded trap), on a
#   model 7x smaller than the one the evaluation was measured on.
#   Two caveats stated rather than buried: a 23 GB GPU cannot hold the 30B eval model, so this is a
#   4B one; and the endpoint serves ONE model, so the verifier is not cross-family here — which D11
#   explicitly argues against. Numbers from this endpoint are NOT comparable to evals/results.jsonl.
#   Cost: an A10G is ~$1.10/hour and scales to zero after 2 minutes idle. No request quota.

# (c) The free tiers. BOTH WERE MEASURED, AND BOTH ARE STRUCTURALLY UNUSABLE FOR THIS AGENT —
#     which is why (b) exists. Stated so nobody repeats the experiment:
#       Groq   — 6,000 tokens/MINUTE. One agent request is ~6,300 tokens. The floor is above the
#                ceiling; this is arithmetic, not throttling.
#       Gemini — 20 requests/DAY per model (free tier). One agent run is ~11 requests. Measured
#                2026-07-14: the agent died at step 8 of the Simpson's task with a 429.
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1                       AGENT_MODEL=qwen/qwen3-32b
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1                         AGENT_MODEL=qwen/qwen3-30b-a3b:free
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/   AGENT_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash

# ─── YOU PROBABLY DO NOT NEED A KEY AT ALL ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# All 8 notebooks replay from the committed response cache with no key and no network:
#
#     from agentlib import set_live
#     set_live(False)
#
# A key is only needed to ask the agent something NEW. Verified from a fresh clone at a foreign
# path, with the environment scrubbed — see D30, which is the bug that made that claim false for
# everyone but me.

# ─── Models (optional overrides) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚠️  Changing AGENT_MODEL invalidates the cache: the model name is in the cache key, so every
#     request becomes a miss and nothing replays. Leave it alone unless you mean to spend money.
# AGENT_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3-30B-A3B-Instruct-2507
# VERIFIER_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
